# The context of deploy/Dockerfile.web, Caddy with the documentation built
# inside it; each image reads the ignore file beside its Dockerfile.
#
# The image installs from the lockfile; a host's node_modules would be the
# largest thing in the context and the wrong platform's binaries.
node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.github
.claude
.local
**/.local

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image.
**/dist
**/.react-router

# A developer's own environment and editor leavings.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
.DS_Store

# Scanner sources have their own Dockerfile-specific contexts. Keep them out
# of this image, except the consent's rules, which the documentation's consent
# banner and page views read from the analytics package's source, with the
# contracts that package names.
/apps/web
/apps/scanner-worker
/apps/browser-observer-actor
/packages/scanner-database
/packages/scanner
/packages/observability
/packages/remediation
/ops
/fixtures
/.env.scanner.example
/.actor
/.actorignore

# Private working material never belongs in an image context.
/06-design/reference
/research
/01-research
/02-meetings
